  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "process_ndpi_collected_info",
    "file": "ndpi/example/reader_util.c",
    "description": "In the TLS/QUIC handling path, process_ndpi_collected_info() duplicates several parser-provided string pointers with strdup() (issuerDN, subjectDN, encrypted_sni.esni) after checking only that the pointer is non-NULL. For this PoV, issuerDN is a non-NULL invalid/wild pointer, so strdup() calls strlen() on attacker-influenced invalid memory and crashes with a SEGV. Root cause is missing pointer validity/ownership guarantees before strdup(), not strdup itself.",
    "conditions": "fuzz_ndpi_reader feeds crafted packet data into ndpi_workflow_process_packet(), which eventually calls packet_processing() and then process_ndpi_collected_info() once flow detection completes. Input must drive flow classification into the TLS/QUIC branch and set tls_quic.issuerDN (or similar duplicated field) to a non-NULL but invalid address. The code then executes strdup(flow->ndpi_flow->protos.tls_quic_stun.tls_quic.issuerDN) at reader_util.c:1207, triggering strlen() on a wild pointer and crashing."
  },
